    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="7" relname="span">I believe intuitiveness refers to ones ability to grasp a concept or manner of accomplishing a task immediately, without first contemplating the how to."</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="1" relname="nonvolitional-cause">This can come, in part, from reminders of past learning experiences or tasks which we keep in memory and can pop up when similar occurrences take place.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="7" relname="means">Intuitiveness in design can be helped by keeping an interface familiar and easy to learn.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="5" relname="joint">One method of measurement could be how long it takes users to successfully navigate a site.</segment>
        <group id="5" type="multinuc"/>
        <group id="6" type="span" parent="5" relname="joint"/>
        <group id="7" type="span" parent="6" relname="span"/>
